{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>and if it seem good</b> — the meaning is good, and like it: which [wine] is good in fittingness [Ecclesiastes 2:3]. The kaf of איככה is doubled, and some say they are two words, like איך, for we find איכה תרה — its meaning is like the meaning of איך. איככה אוכל להיות — [for it to be]. The nun of באבדן is in place of mem, or it is feminine diction, and the meaning is destruction of persons of my kindred. And it is better that באבדן be a verbal noun, like מכת חרב והרג ואבדן, and the nun is added, for the patterns of verbal nouns vary."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:16.166635125Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}